<article class="env-definition" id="0H5R">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H5R">Definition <span data-tag="0H5R">62.9.1</span>.</a> Let $f : X \to S$ be a morphism of schemes. Assume $S$ is locally Noetherian and $f$ is locally of finite type. Let $r \geq 0$ be an integer. We say a relative $r$-cycle $\alpha $ on $X/S$ <em>effective</em> if $\alpha _ s$ is an effective cycle (Chow Homology, Definition <a href="/tag/0H47" data-tag="0H47">42.8.4</a>) for all $s \in S$. The monoid of all effective relative $r$-cycles on $X/S$ is denoted $z^{eff}(X/S, r)$. </p>
</article>